---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { offersActive } from '../data/offers';

const title = 'Getting to Mikumi from Dar es Salaam & Zanzibar | Camp Lilac';
const description =
  'Dar es Salaam to Mikumi by SGR train (1.5 h to Morogoro plus our 2 h transfer), by road (5–6 h), from Zanzibar by ferry or flight, or by air. Timings and costs.';
// No HowTo schema: Google dropped HowTo rich results in 2023, so it only added noise here.
---

<Base {title} {description} breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Getting here', href: '/getting-here' }]}>
  <div class="wrap page-head">
    <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Getting here</p>
    <h1>Getting to Camp Lilac, Mikumi</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Mikumi is the easiest safari park to reach in Tanzania. Here is every way to get here from Dar es Salaam, Zanzibar and
      the south, with honest timings.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap split--aside" style="display:grid">
    <article class="article">
      <Photo src="/images/rooms/mv-cabin-3-1600.jpg" alt="The Mountain View Cabin at Camp Lilac, the end of the journey from Dar es Salaam" caption="Arrival" ratio="landscape" loading="eager" />

      <h2 id="train">Option 1: SGR train from Dar es Salaam (recommended)</h2>
      <p>
        The standard-gauge railway runs several times a day between Dar es Salaam and Morogoro, taking about 1.5 hours in
        air-conditioned comfort. From Morogoro station it is a 2-hour drive to the camp. Our driver meets you on the
        platform with a name board.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Tickets:</strong> buy in the TRC app or at the station; economy and business class. Book a few days ahead in high season and over holidays.</li>
        <li><strong>Timing:</strong> take a morning train and you can be on an afternoon game drive the same day.</li>
        <li><strong>Our transfer:</strong> Morogoro station → camp, about 2 hours.{offersActive && <span data-offer> <strong>Free one way</strong> with a 2-day safari booked direct for November 2026. With a 3- or 4-day safari we also pay your train ticket from Dar es Salaam. The return journey is charged.</span>} Booking a room only? Then the transfer is charged — ask us for the price.</li>
        <li><strong>Kilosa station:</strong> a stop closer to the park is being developed; for now Morogoro is the practical choice.</li>
        <li><strong>Step by step:</strong> our <a href="/blog/dar-es-salaam-to-mikumi-by-sgr-train">SGR train guide</a> walks through tickets, timings and the pickup. For the whole trip as a package, see <a href="/safari-from-dar-es-salaam">safari from Dar es Salaam</a> and the <a href="/safaris/2-day-mikumi-safari">2-Day Mikumi Safari</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="road">Option 2: By road from Dar es Salaam (not our recommendation)</h2>
      <p>
        About 300 km on the A7 (Morogoro Road). Count 5–6 hours to Morogoro including leaving Dar es Salaam, longer on Fridays and holidays, and then 2 more hours to Mikumi. Compared with the train, a transfer car is more expensive, slower and much more tiring — the train does the Dar–Morogoro leg in 1.5 hours — so we recommend the road only if the train times do not fit.
        We arrange private transfers from Dar es Salaam hotels or Julius Nyerere International Airport, and the road passes
        through the Mikumi park itself for the last stretch — your first wildlife sightings are often from the car.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Private transfer:</strong> door to door, flexible times; price on request.</li>
        <li><strong>Bus:</strong> buses to Iringa and Mbeya stop in Mikumi town; we can collect you there.</li>
        <li><strong>Self-drive:</strong> a normal car is fine for the highway; the camp track is passable in all seasons. Do not drive the park section after dark.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="zanzibar">Option 3: From Zanzibar</h2>
      <p>
        Take the 07:00 fast ferry from Stone Town to Dar es Salaam (about 2 hours), then either the SGR train to Morogoro with
        our pickup, or a private road transfer from the ferry terminal. You arrive in time for dinner facing the Mikumi mountain ridge and a
        dawn game drive the next morning. Prefer to fly? A short flight takes you from Zanzibar to Dar es Salaam (US$160–200 per person each way, depending on the day and the airline; not included), or a light aircraft can fly you straight to the Mikumi airstrip. We book ferries and flights for you and meet you on arrival. Many guests do Mikumi as a 2–3 night break from the beach.
      </p>
      <p>
        The whole trip, with timings, prices and a worked example, is on our <a href="/safari-from-zanzibar">safari from Zanzibar</a> page; most guests take the <a href="/safaris/2-day-mikumi-safari">2-Day Mikumi Safari</a> or the <a href="/safaris/3-day-mikumi-safari">3-Day Mikumi Safari</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="air">Option 4: By air</h2>
      <p>
        Charter flights can land at the Mikumi airstrip. Scheduled flights serve Iringa (about 3 hours by road) and Dar es Salaam.
        For most travellers the train is faster door to door and far cheaper.
      </p>

      <h2 id="south">Coming from the south (Iringa, Ruaha, Mbeya)</h2>
      <p>
        Camp Lilac sits just off the highway between the south and Dar es Salaam, which makes it a natural overnight stop
        after Ruaha or Iringa. Arrive by late afternoon for an evening game drive and leave after breakfast.
      </p>

      <h2>Airport pickups</h2>
      <p>
        We offer pickups at Julius Nyerere International Airport (Dar es Salaam) and at Morogoro SGR station. Send us your
        flight or train number when you book and we take care of the rest. Pickups are charged{offersActive && <span data-offer>, except the free one-way
        Morogoro transfer that comes with a November 2026 safari of 2 days or more</span>}.
      </p>
    </article>

    <aside class="aside">
      <h3>Transfers at a glance</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Morogoro SGR station ↔ camp: 2 h</li>
        <li>Dar es Salaam ↔ camp: 5–6 h by road</li>
        <li>Airport and station pickups (charged for room-only stays)</li>
        {offersActive && <li data-offer>November 2026 — 2-day safari: free one-way transfer Morogoro → Mikumi (worth US$75)</li>}{offersActive && <li data-offer>November 2026 — 3- or 4-day safari: free economy train tickets Dar → Morogoro + transfer (one way)</li>}<li><a href="/offers">{offersActive ? 'See the safari deals' : 'Why book direct'}</a></li>
      </ul>
      <a class="btn btn--fill" href="/book">Request a transfer</a>
      <p style="margin-top:12px;font-size:0.9rem"><a href={site.whatsapp}>WhatsApp us</a> for same-day questions.</p>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <CtaBand />
</Base>
